{"addedOn":10,"avgRating":["fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o"],"breadcrumbsHtml":"<a href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117\">OpenEdge Development: ABL Reference</a>\n<span><i class=\"fa fa-angle-right\"></i>\n</span>\n<a href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/ABL-Syntax-Reference.html\">ABL Syntax Reference</a>\n<span><i class=\"fa fa-angle-right\"></i>\n</span>\n<span class=\"active\">DYNAMIC-ENUM function</span>\n","class":"manual","created":1470,"dislikeurl":"https://docs-be.progress.com/dislike/309363","html":"<article class=\"hascomments\" data-page=\"bundle:openedge-abl-reference-117/enus/DYNAMIC-ENUM-function.html\" id=\"bundle:openedge-abl-reference-117/enus/DYNAMIC-ENUM-function.html\"><main role=\"main\"><article aria-labelledby=\"ariaid-title1\" class=\"dita\" id=\"DYNAMIC-ENUM-function\" role=\"article\">\n  <h1 class=\"title topictitle1 reference\" id=\"ariaid-title1\">DYNAMIC-ENUM function</h1>\n  \n  <div class=\"body refbody\">\n    <section class=\"section\">\n      <p class=\"p\">Returns an instance of the enumeration type for the specified enumeration member. </p>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"DYNAMIC-ENUM-function__syntax_GC17HT2690617\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d203140e96\">Syntax</h2>\n      \n      <table class=\"table frame-all\" id=\"DYNAMIC-ENUM-function__idGDK2B02668980\"><caption></caption><colgroup><col style=\"width:100%\" /></colgroup><tbody class=\"tbody\">\n            <tr class=\"row rowsep-0\">\n              <td class=\"entry colsep-1 rowsep-1\">\n                <pre class=\"pre codeblock\"><code><strong class=\"ph b synmeta\">[</strong> <var class=\"keyword varname\">return-value</var> = <strong class=\"ph b synmeta\">]</strong> DYNAMIC-ENUM( <var class=\"keyword varname\">enum-type-name</var>, <var class=\"keyword varname\">enum-member</var> )</code></pre>\n               \n                \n              </td>\n            </tr>\n          </tbody></table>\n      <dl class=\"dl parml\">\n        \n          <dt class=\"dt pt dlterm\">\n            <var class=\"keyword varname\">return-value</var>\n          </dt>\n          <dd class=\"dd pd\">Specifies a data element that is assigned the returned value. The AVM checks that the\n            enum instance returned can be assigned to the target, and the AVM raises an error if the\n            data types aren&#39;t compatible.</dd>\n        \n        \n          <dt class=\"dt pt dlterm\">\n            <var class=\"keyword varname\">enum-type-name</var>\n          </dt>\n          <dd class=\"dd pd\">Specifies the name of an ABL or .NET enumeration type that defines the member. This is\n            a CHARACTER expression that the AVM evaluates to the type name of an enumeration type at\n            runtime. </dd>\n        \n        \n          <dt class=\"dt pt dlterm\">\n            <var class=\"keyword varname\">enum-member</var>\n          </dt>\n          <dd class=\"dd pd\">Specifies an enum member in one of two ways:<ul class=\"ul\">\n              <li class=\"li\">A CHARACTER expression that evaluates to the member name at runtime. For flag\n                enums, this can be a comma-delimited list of member names for two or more members\n                defined by the enum type.</li>\n              <li class=\"li\">An INTEGER or INT64 expression that evaluates to the underlying numeric value of\n                the member at runtime. For flag enums, this numeric value can represent two or more\n                members defined by the enum type.</li>\n            </ul><div class=\"note note note_note\"><span class=\"note__title\">Note:</span> The function generates a runtime error if any specified character or numeric\n              value does not correspond to a defined member.</div></dd>\n        \n      </dl>\n      \n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d203140e185\">Example</h2>\n      \n      <p class=\"p\">In the following code fragment, <code class=\"ph codeph\">Direction</code> is an enum with a member defined\n        for each of the four cardinal directions (see the <a class=\"xref\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"ENUM-statement.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/ENUM-statement.html\">ENUM statement</a> for an\n        example of how <code class=\"ph codeph\">Direction</code> could be defined), and\n          <code class=\"ph codeph\">cNeededDirection</code> is a string that evaluates to the name of one of the\n        members defined by <code class=\"ph codeph\">Direction</code>. The code then uses DYAMIC-ENUM to set\n          <code class=\"ph codeph\">myDirection</code> as an object reference to an instance of the member specified\n        by <code class=\"ph codeph\">cNeededDirection</code>:</p>\n      <table class=\"table frame-all\"><caption></caption><colgroup><col style=\"width:100%\" /></colgroup><tbody class=\"tbody\">\n            <tr class=\"row rowsep-0\">\n              <td class=\"entry colsep-1 rowsep-1\">\n                <pre class=\"pre codeblock\"><code>DEFINE INPUT PARAMETER cNeededDirection AS CHARACTER.\nDEFINE VARIABLE myDirection AS Direction.\n\nmyDirection = DYNAMIC-ENUM(&quot;Direction&quot;, cNeededDirection).</code></pre>\n                \n                \n              </td>\n            </tr>\n          </tbody></table>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"DYNAMIC-ENUM-function__see-also_GC17HU2690643\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d203140e237\">See also</h2>\n      \n      <p class=\"p\">\n        <a class=\"xref\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"ENUM-statement.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/ENUM-statement.html\">ENUM statement</a></p>\n    </section>\n    \n  </div>\n<nav role=\"navigation\"><div class=\"familylinks\"><div class=\"previouslink\"><strong>Previous topic:</strong> <a class=\"link\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"DYNAMIC-CURRENT-VALUE-statement.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/DYNAMIC-CURRENT-VALUE-statement.html\">DYNAMIC-CURRENT-VALUE statement</a></div><div class=\"nextlink\"><strong>Next topic:</strong> <a class=\"link\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"DYNAMIC-FUNCTION-function.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/DYNAMIC-FUNCTION-function.html\">DYNAMIC-FUNCTION function</a></div></div></nav><nav class=\"related-links\" role=\"navigation\"></nav></article></main></article>\n","isWatched":false,"labelText":"Product; Product > OpenEdge; Product > OpenEdge > Version 11.7; Format; Format > Documentation","likes":0,"likeurl":"https://docs-be.progress.com/like/309363","myDocsURL":null,"numOfPageViews":0,"numOfRatingsText":"<span>0 Ratings","revised":1470,"showWatch":false,"topicMeta":[["bookowner","oe11docs"],["bookrights","oe11docs"],["bundle","openedge-abl-reference-117"],["data","OEInformationHub/Product"],["data","OEInformationHub/Product/product_openedge"],["data","OEInformationHub/Product/product_openedge/product_openedge_117"],["data","OEInformationHub/format"],["data","OEInformationHub/format/format_documentation"],["organization","oe11docs"]],"topicTitle":"DYNAMIC-ENUM function","topicurl":"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/DYNAMIC-ENUM-function.html","type":"Manual"}